      "resourceNotes": "<p>Factories are treated one resource class lower when calculating sector resource class.</p><p>Factories increase income from resources with the housing tag in the sector by 10%, minimum 1.</p><p>Factories produce a specific type of good integrated into a supply chain. They do not allow you to purchase the items they create, but they lower item costs through normal channels.</p><p>Factory type effects:</p><ul><li>Consumer Good: increase market cap by 10%, minimum 1.</li><li>Vehicle: reduce vehicle costs by 30%.</li><li>Industrial: reduce cyberware costs by 10%.</li><li>Munitions: decrease firearms costs by 30%.</li><li>Chemical: reduce drugs/injectibles/medicine costs by 90%.</li></ul>",
